The Laboratory: a 2-minute stereo record buffer played as a loop, recorded
and reset like the granular looper's. Runs at 96 kHz (the sound chip's
highest rate) with a JACK block of 128. Source: source/ (looper.h is the
sound). Only the lines between nebconfigbegin and nebconfigend are read.

  record   on: a new take from the beginning of the buffer, heard live while
           it records. Off: the take ends, the loop plays from start. Past
           2 minutes it records on circularly: the take is the last 2 minutes.
  reset    (button or gate) the playhead jumps to start.
  file + reset   hold file, press reset: the buffer is cleared (as on the
           granular looper). While recording, the take starts again.
  start    where the loop starts, 0..1 of the take (knob + CV). The loop
           runs from start to the end of the take.
  speed    max = normal speed forward, min = normal speed backward, middle
           = stopped (snaps to exactly normal speed near the ends). The speed
           LEDs show it as the granular looper does: right = forward, left =
           backward, bright blue = normal speed, bright yellow = half, orange
           = 1/4, white = 1/8 (speedleds,playback).
  blend    dry/wet: left = the input, right = the loop.

Jumps (reset, the loop's end) fade over 5 ms, so they do not click.

nebconfigbegin
run,thelaboratory
oscport,3023
kernel,any
blocksize,128
-r,96000
record,latching,rising
reset,triggered,rising
filestate,momentary,rising
osc:record,/lab/record,0,1
osc:reset,/lab/reset,0,1
osc:filestate,/lab/file_held,0,1
osc:start,/lab/start,0,1
osc:speed,/lab/speed,-1,1
speedleds,playback
osc:blend,/lab/mix,0,1
nebconfigend
